# Line endings are normalised to LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout and every text
# file in the repository shows as modified — a three-file change reads as a
# forty-file diff, and cherry-picking a commit back to TEMPLATE-OPEN-EDITION
# becomes impractical.
#
# LF also matches what the template shipped and what the Netlify build runs on,
# so this keeps the fork, the template and the deploy target in agreement.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and generated assets Git should never try to normalise.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
